From 6c8f33e7d79048387631a5caf473f8d9c3258996 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:13:42 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban remote: Desktop sweep stands aside while the
 gateway's turn holds a chat (t_01a1cff0541bf30c G3)

Live G3 failure after PR #1486 (MacBook, Nov 13 02:24-03:51 PST): the tui backend's remote sweep
(every 15-25 s) reached busy gateway-owned chat f07c32 before the gateway's owner pass. It claimed
each remote notice, failed the passive row on the turn lease, released it and logged
"deferred: a turn is running" up to 6 times in a row per notice (t_01a1d46fe87dff26: 6,
03:36:31-03:37:58).

Five whys:
1. Deferred lines: the sweep claimed while a turn ran and append_kanban_notice raised
   SessionTurnLeaseLostError (kanban_remote_notices._persist_claimed).
2. It claimed because it stands aside only once a gateway admission holds the key
   (kanban_remote_fifo.gateway_holds); before the gateway's next pass it keeps trying.
3. The gateway pass came 13-88 s later (it runs inside the notifier loop), and a sweep claim held
   through a wake makes the owner's collect skip the notice.
Root (happened): custody hand-off keyed on "an admission exists", not "the live gateway's turn
holds the chat". Root (not caught): N1/N2 drove tick(force=True) alone, never with the sweep.

Fix (review t_01a1d4c44f637fff, approve-with-changes): _deliver_link stands aside, with no claim,
no wake and one wait line per episode, while an UNEXPIRED turn lease on the chat's lineage is held
by the canonical gateway's verified pid (live_gateway_pid_for_home for the link profile, else the
multiplexed default gateway; never discover_owner). While that lease is held neither the passive
row nor a desktop wake can land, so nothing deliverable is given up. An expired lease (the passive
row guard reclaims it even from a live pid), a dead holder or a non-gateway holder keep today's
path. Lease-only on purpose: no ledger arm. The owner pass's own cadence (review item B) is split
to its own latency card.

Tests: tests/gateway/test_kanban_remote_lease_stand_aside.py (stand-aside with no claim/no
deferred, no owner pass -> exactly one delivery after release, dead holder, expired lease,
non-gateway holder, pid lookup fallback).
